  "answer_text": "**\"Still in Love with You\"** is a deep-cut country song by the legendary duo **Brooks & Dunn**. \n\n### Key Song Facts\n* **Album:** It is the 10th and final track on their massively successful debut studio album, ***Brand New Man***, released on August 13, 1991. \n* **Writers:** Kix Brooks, Ronnie Dunn, and Don Cook.\n* **Producers:** Don Cook and Scott Hendricks.\n\n---\n\n### Lyrics\nHere are the lyrics to the song:\n\n**(Verse 1)**\nMy taxicab is waiting\nWish I could hold you one last time\nAfter all we've had together\nThere's gotta be a better way\nOf telling you goodbye\n\n**(Chorus)**\nIf I had a horse, I'd ride off in the sunset\nIf I had wings, I'd fly off in the sky so blue\nIf I had the time, I'd spend my whole life dreaming\nBut I'd wake up, still in love with you\n\n**(Verse 2)**\nBe in Baton Rouge by morning\nHope you're missing me by then\nI'd like to be the kind of memory\nThat makes you want to take me back\nIn your arms again\n\n**(Chorus)**\nIf I had a horse, I'd ride off in the sunset\nIf I had wings, I'd fly off in the sky so blue\nIf I had the time, I'd spend my whole life dreaming\nBut I'd wake up, still in love with you\n\n**(Bridge)**\nSome nights when you get lonely\nWill you still remember me?\n\n**(Chorus - Key Change)**\nIf I had a horse, I'd ride off in the sunset\nIf I had wings, I'd fly off in the sky so blue\nIf I had the time, I'd spend my whole life dreaming\nBut I'd wake up, still in love with you\nYes, I'd wake up, still in love with you",
